  "name": "Calung (Sundanese struck bamboo tubes)",
  "family": "global",
  "lineage": "Sundanese music for calung, tuned bamboo tubes struck with a mallet (here the bamboo tube-xylophone card), either strung on a cord (calung rantay) or fixed on a hand-held frame (calung jinjing). From 1960 arts activists at Universitas Padjadjaran in Bandung developed calung jinjing, each player carrying one, into a stage entertainment of songs and comic banter that the singer Darso later carried onto pop Sunda cassettes.",
